// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Two checks with the same condition and opposite verdicts, with main written
// before the procedure it calls. The compiler lays out procedures before main,
// so the result lists f's check first while the source has main's first. Each
// report row carries its check's own source position as its label, so each
// verdict lands on its line; pairing rows with checks by order of occurrence
// would swap the two.
//
// Concretely x is 1 at main's check and 2 at f's (x is local to each).
fun main() {
  x = 1;
  __voblint_check(x == 1); // PROVED
  f();
}
fun f() {
  x = 2;
  __voblint_check(x == 1); // REFUTED
}
